            {
                "post_id": "post_a13b3263",
                "title": "Wildlife Population Update — April 2026 Release",
                "body": "We are pleased to share the latest verified population figures from our Q1 2026 Northern Range surveys, drawn from the official April 15, 2026 dataset release (v1.0).\n\n🐺 Gray Wolf — Estimated population: 428 individuals\n🦊 Red Fox — Estimated population: 1,260 individuals\n\nBoth datasets (wds_gray_wolf_2026_04_15 and wds_red_fox_2026_04_15) have been confirmed as the current approved release, verified for publication, and sourced from FanaticWildlifeViews.com. These figures reflect survey data collected during Q1 2026 across the Northern Range region.\n\nWe will continue to monitor population trends and share updates as new survey data becomes available. Thank you for your continued support of wildlife conservation efforts.",
                "published_at": "2026-11-01T01:51:45.766650Z",
                "channel": "conservation_blog"
